  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 118 PM CDT Fri Jun 19 2026\n\nA flat upper level ridge will be over the area through much of the \nlong term. That means mainly hot and dry conditions, especially \nacross the southern half of the area. Highs will be in the 90s \nacross much of the area with 100 to 104 across the western Big \nCountry and western Concho Valley Sunday and Monday. Across the Big \nCountry, a few weak disturbances aloft will bring a few rounds of \nscattered thunderstorms(low to medium rain chances Monday night). \nAlso, there is an marginal risk for excessive rainfall across the \nBig Country Monday and Tuesday. The severe weather risk looks very \nlow to low at this time.",
